## Why This Is Asked
Real-world systems must balance cost and performance in multi-tenant AI deployments. This question probes how to design routing, quota enforcement, caching, and versioned prompts with auditable tracing.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-tenant prompt routing and model selection
- Cost awareness and latency SLA compliance
- Per-tenant quotas and burst handling
- Prompt versioning stored in Blob with Cognitive Search
- RBAC with Azure AD and end-to-end tracing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Skeleton: chooseModel for a tenant
async function chooseModel(tenantId, latencyBudgetMs, quotas, pricing) {
  // Check quota, burst lock
  // Pick cheapest model meeting latency
  // Consider cached prompt variant
  return { model: "gpt-3.5-turbo", cost: pricing["gpt-3.5-turbo"] };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate SLAs across tenants under varying load?
- How would you design tests for cache invalidation when prompts are upgraded?

## Why This Is Asked
Demonstrates practical API boundary design, basic rate limiting, and graceful degradation in a beginner-friendly Azure setup.

## Key Concepts
- API Management quotas and rate limits by user
- Per-user spend cap and simple state store
- Fallback to rule-based replies on failure
- Observability for quotas and failures

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal mock of request flow with quota check and fallback
async function handle(req) {
  const user = req.userId;
  const quota = getUserQuota(user);
  if (quota.remaining <= 0) return cannedReply();
  try {
    const res = await callOpenAI(req.payload);
    debitQuota(user, req.payload.length);
    return res;
  } catch {
    return cannedReply();
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test quota expiry and fallback paths?
- How would you simulate OpenAI downtime in a local test environment?

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes designing a scalable, compliant incident-response assistant that isolates tenants, enforces cost controls, and integrates with Azure Monitor, Cognitive Search, RBAC, and auditing.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant sandboxed OpenAI deployments behind API Management
- Event-driven ingestion from Azure Monitor
- KB grounding via Cognitive Search
- PII redaction with Text Analytics
- RBAC with Azure AD and Data Lake auditing
- Canary rollout and end-to-end tests

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo routing function outline
async function handleIncident(event) {
  const tenant = extractTenant(event);
  const doc = await kbSearch(tenant, event);
  const prompt = buildPrompt(doc, event);
  const redacted = redactPII(prompt);
  const res = await openaiQuery(tenant, redacted);
  await logAudit(tenant, event, res);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test for latency under peak load?
- How would you ensure data residency per tenant across regions?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design a privacy-preserving, multi-tenant AI workflow at scale, with strict data isolation, governance, and measurable latency.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant OpenAI deployment and prompt routing
- Real-time ingestion (Event Hubs) and low-latency scoring
- KB grounding via Cognitive Search on Blob data
- PII redaction (Text Analytics) and per-tenant masking (Key Vault)
- RBAC (Azure AD), Data Lake auditing, canary rollout

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: route prompt for tenant, redact, ground, respond
async function handleRequest(req){
  const tenantId = req.headers['x-tenant'];
  const raw = req.body;
  const redacted = redactPII(raw);
  const kb = loadKBVersion(tenantId);
  const prompt = buildPrompt(redacted, kb, tenantId);
  const resp = await openai.complete(prompt, {deployment: getDeployment(tenantId)});
  logAudit(tenantId, prompt, resp);
  return resp;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How to quantify latency vs. isolation trade-offs?
- How to implement drift detection for the KB and prompts across tenants?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of Azure OpenAI deployment, API management, knowledge-grounding, data privacy, and governance in a realistic, beginner-friendly setting.

## Key Concepts
- Azure OpenAI Service integration with gateway
- Knowledge-grounding via Azure Cognitive Search
- PII redaction with Text Analytics
- Per-repo policy gating and audit logging to Data Lake

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: redactPII and gate before OpenAI call
function handleRequest(req){
  const redacted = redactPII(req.input);
  if (!policyAllows(req.repo, redacted)) return denyResponse();
  return callOpenAI({input:redacted});
}
```

